    "details": "<h1>OpenCode '26 &ndash; Events &amp; Prize Details</h1>\n<p>Get ready for a month filled with technology, creativity, gaming, competition, and exciting opportunities!</p>\n<h2>About OpenCode</h2>\n<p><strong>OpenCode '26</strong>, organized by GeekHaven, IIIT Allahabad, is a month-long open-source hackathon designed to help students begin or advance their journey in open source.</p>\n<p>Inspired by innovation, collaboration, and continuous improvement, OpenCode provides a platform for students to explore new technologies, contribute to real-world projects, enhance their technical skills, and connect with the open-source community.</p>\n<p>Whether you are a beginner or an experienced developer, OpenCode offers opportunities to learn, build, collaborate, and showcase your skills.</p>\n<h2>Domains &amp; Tech Stacks</h2>\n<p>Explore projects and contribute across multiple domains:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Web Development:</strong> React, Node.js, Express, MongoDB, Spring Boot</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>App Development:</strong> Flutter, Kotlin</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Design:</strong> Figma, UI/UX, Prototyping, Wireframing, Typography</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>AI/ML:</strong> Python, PyTorch, TensorFlow, LLaMA</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Cybersecurity</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Game Development:</strong> Unity</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Blockchain</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Main OpenCode Leaderboard Prizes</h2>\n<p>The main OpenCode winners will be announced in <strong>two phases</strong>:</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Winner Announcement</th>\n<th>Duration</th>\n<th>Prize Pool</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>December Winners</td>\n<td>2 Weeks</td>\n<td>₹10,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>January Winners</td>\n<td>3 Weeks</td>\n<td>₹20,000</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td><strong>5 Weeks</strong></td>\n<td><strong>₹30,000</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Winners will be determined based on their performance and rankings on the official OpenCode leaderboard.</p>\n<h2>Sub-Events &amp; Competitions</h2>\n<p>Apart from the main open-source contribution program, several exciting sub-events will take place:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>CSS Battle</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>CC Wing Contest</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Brand Rebrand</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Data Blitz</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>App Dev Event</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Separate Sub-Event Winners</h2>\n<p>Each sub-event will have its own winners and separate prize distribution.</p>\n<p>These prizes are independent of the main OpenCode leaderboard rewards, providing participants with multiple opportunities to compete and win throughout the event.</p>\n<h2>Participation &amp; Guidelines</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Individual participation only; team participation is not allowed.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>All project contributions and Pull Requests must be submitted through GitHub.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Participants should follow the respective repository's contribution guidelines.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Submissions should maintain proper project structure, documentation, and meaningful commit messages.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Participants must maintain a respectful, inclusive, and collaborative environment on GitHub and Discord.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Plagiarism and misrepresentation of contributions are strictly prohibited.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Contributions will be assessed based on code quality, creativity, implementation, technical execution, and overall impact. Specific issue points and evaluation criteria will be communicated by project mentors.</p>\n<h2>Registration &amp; Community Links</h2>\n<p>Participants must complete registration and join the official community to participate and stay updated.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>OpenCode Leaderboard Portal:</strong> <a href=\"https://events.geekhaven.in/\">https://events.geekhaven.in/</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Official Discord Server:</strong> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/42JXjtERD\">https://discord.gg/42JXjtERD</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Registration on both Unstop and the OpenCode Leaderboard Portal is mandatory.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Leaderboard portal registration is essential for contribution tracking and awarding points.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Joining the Discord server is mandatory for announcements, communication, and mentorship support.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div><hr /></div>\n<p><strong>Multiple Events. Multiple Winners. Bigger Opportunities!</strong></p>\n<p>Keep Learning. Keep Building. Keep Improving.</p>\n<p>See you at OpenCode '26!</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Detailed rules, issue-allocation procedures, contribution guidelines, and participation instructions are provided in the attached Official Participant Rulebook.</p>",
